# ============================================================================
# Local development credentials for docker-compose
# ============================================================================
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored (see .gitignore:6). Never commit it. Never put a
# production credential in it - the compose stack is local-only, and a
# workstation holding production database credentials is a standing risk.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There are intentionally no committed defaults
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every variable below is REQUIRED and has no fallback anywhere in the repo.
# docker-compose declares each one as `${VAR:?message}`, so `docker compose up`
# stops immediately with a named error if one is missing, and
# scripts/mongo-init.js throws rather than creating a database user with a
# default password.
#
# That strictness is the point. This repository previously shipped working
# credentials - `admin` / `password123` in docker-compose.yml and CI, and
# `foodwaste_user` / `foodwaste_password` in scripts/mongo-init.js. They
# survived because they worked: five integration suites hardcoded the same
# string as a fallback, so the compose password could not be changed without
# breaking the test suite. A weak default that silently works is more dangerous
# than a startup error, because nothing ever forces anyone to look at it.
#
# The placeholder values below are deliberately NOT usable. Replace them.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generating strong values
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(24).toString('base64url'))"
#
# Run it once per secret. Do not reuse one value across two variables.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WARNING - existing local volumes
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MONGO_INITDB_ROOT_USERNAME and MONGO_INITDB_ROOT_PASSWORD are read by the
# mongo image ONLY when the data volume is created for the first time. If you
# already have a local stack, the previous credentials are baked into that
# volume and anything you set here will fail authentication instead of taking
# effect. Recreate the volume before switching:
#
#   docker compose down -v && docker compose up -d
#
# `-v` destroys local database contents. It touches nothing remote.
# ============================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MongoDB root account
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Consumed by: the mongodb service (MONGO_INITDB_ROOT_*), the mongo-init
# service that initiates the replica set, the backend's DATABASE_URL, and
# mongo-express.
MONGO_ROOT_USERNAME=CHANGE_ME_local_root_user
MONGO_ROOT_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_generate_with_the_command_above

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MongoDB application account
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Consumed by: scripts/mongo-init.js, which creates this user against the
# `foodwaste` database with readWrite + dbAdmin, and by mongo-express, which
# connects with it rather than with the root account.
MONGO_APP_USERNAME=CHANGE_ME_local_app_user
MONGO_APP_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_generate_with_the_command_above

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# JWT signing secrets
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Must be at least 32 characters, must differ from each other, and must not be
# any of the known development literals - env.validation.ts rejects all three
# conditions at startup. Generate a fresh pair per environment:
#
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('hex'))"
JWT_SECRET=CHANGE_ME_generate_a_unique_64_char_hex_secret
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=CHANGE_ME_generate_a_DIFFERENT_64_char_hex_secret

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local admin UIs - ONLY needed for the opt-in overlay
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Grafana, mongo-express and redis-commander live in docker-compose.tools.yml
# and do not start with a plain `docker compose up`. You only need the four
# values below if you run:
#
#   docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.tools.yml up -d
#
# All three bind to 127.0.0.1 only. Do not expose them off localhost.
# GRAFANA_ADMIN_USERNAME=
# GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# MONGO_EXPRESS_USERNAME=
# MONGO_EXPRESS_PASSWORD=
# REDIS_COMMANDER_USERNAME=
# REDIS_COMMANDER_PASSWORD=

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Integration test suites
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `pnpm --filter @foodwaste/backend test:db` requires MONGO_TEST_URI and has no
# default (test/helpers/mongo-test-uri.ts). Build it from the root account
# above once the stack is up:
#
#   MONGO_TEST_URI="mongodb://$MONGO_ROOT_USERNAME:$MONGO_ROOT_PASSWORD@localhost:27017/admin?replicaSet=rs0&directConnection=true"
#
# Left commented out on purpose: the suites should fail loudly when it is
# unset rather than quietly connect somewhere unexpected.
# MONGO_TEST_URI=
